---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const notebook = "/notebooks/marimo/index.html";
const editor = "/notebooks/marimo/edit.html";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Counting photons — an interactive notebook"
  description="Explore photon counting noise with a Python notebook that runs in your browser."
>
  <article class="experiment">
    <header class="intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Notebook experiment <span>01 / marimo</span></p>
      <h1>A little light.<br />A lot of randomness.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Even a perfectly steady source flickers in the data. Count its photons,
        change its brightness, and see where the noise comes from.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="notebook" aria-label="Interactive photon-counting notebook">
      <div class="notebook-bar">
        <span class="status"><span aria-hidden="true">●</span> Python in your browser</span>
        <a href={editor} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Edit the code ↗</a>
      </div>
      <iframe
        src={notebook}
        title="Counting photons: interactive marimo notebook"
        height="960"
      ></iframe>
    </section>

    <div class="afterword">
      <p>
        Move either slider to run the calculation again. To change the experiment
        itself, open <a href={editor} target="_blank" rel="noopener">the notebook editor</a>
        and press ▶ to run its cells. Your edits stay in your browser; download
        a copy to keep them.
      </p>
      <p class="note">
        The first launch downloads Python and may take a moment. An internet
        connection and JavaScript are required.
        <a href={notebook} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the experiment on its own ↗</a>
      </p>
      <a class="back" href="/blog/">← Back to the blog</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .experiment {
    width: min(100% - 2 * var(--gutter), 66rem);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem);
  }

  .intro, .afterword {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin-block-end: 1.5rem;
  }

  .eyebrow span { color: var(--fog-400); }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 6vw, 4.2rem); line-height: 1.1; }
  .lede { margin-block-start: 1.5rem; color: var(--fog-300); font-size: var(--step-1); }

  .notebook {
    margin-block: 2.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--ink-900);
  }

  .notebook-bar {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .status { color: var(--fog-300); }
  .status span { color: var(--gold); margin-inline-end: 0.5rem; }
  iframe { display: block; width: 100%; border: 0; background: #18181b; }
  .afterword p + p { margin-block-start: 1rem; }
  .note { color: var(--fog-400); font-size: var(--step--1); }
  .note a { display: inline-block; margin-inline-start: 0.25em; }
  .back { display: inline-block; margin-block-start: 2rem; }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    iframe { height: 1080px; }
  }
</style>
